# =============================================================================
# d64 increment — postfix ↑/↓ reject on decimal operands
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Postfix `↑`/`↓` take integer operands only (Q-L4 ruling, 2026-10-15).
#     On a `d64` the runner would otherwise add one 10^-8 carrier unit
#     (1.5 → 1.50000001), wrong under the decimal model.
#   • The operand fails closed at check time with
#     `SEM011:postfix_inc_dec_numerus_operand`, the same diagnostic a float
#     operand gets.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • incrementing money — increment an `int`, or write `d ← d + 1.0`
#
# See also: numerus, d64
# =============================================================================

# decimal/increment-reject — d64 is not an integer operand
#
# WHY: one carrier unit is not the value one; `↑` would silently corrupt a
# decimal, so it must reject, as it does for floats.

main {
    mut d64 d ← 1.5
    d ↑
}
